Assembly Manager 20262835 
 - SALARY INDICATION In consultation - FUNCTION GROUP Engineering - JOB POSTING NUMBER 20262835 - LOCATION Valkenswaard ABOUT THIS JOB OPENING The Position 
Your role is to coordinate, manage, and improve the activities of the assembly department-not only in terms of the assembly process itself, but also in the areas of safety, quality, output, and hygiene. You are responsible for work planning and task allocation to ensure that work proceeds according to schedule. In addition, you translate company objectives into clear actions on the shop floor and actively involve employees in the organization of (production) processes and their further optimization. A key focus of the role is therefore coaching, motivating, inspiring, and developing employees to build support for working according to (new) agreements. In short, you are a people manager through and through. You will lead a team of production employees (approximately 25 people). 
Your duties and responsibilities include the following: 
Managing the daily assembly process and ensuring the organization, planning, coordination, and facilitation of optimal work execution; 
Reporting on and monitoring productivity, costs, and quality, among other things; 
Ensuring optimal utilization and effectiveness of production resources and further professionalizing these processes; 
Taking the initiative to improve quality and productivity; 
Maintaining contact with support departments and external parties; 
Supervising and ensuring workplace safety. 
We are looking for 
Completed (technical) MBO+ or HBO education; 
At least 2-4 years of managerial experience in a production environment; 
Knowledge of the mechanical engineering industry is a major plus; 
Proficiency in Dutch and English; 
Experience with implementing, defining, and improving assembly processes; 
Good knowledge of computer applications (including the WMS system); 
Strong communication skills and the abili...

The position
As an electrician, you will work in a team of over 40 technicians as part of Technical Services. You will independently carry out repairs, maintenance, commissioning and periodic safety inspections of electrical construction machinery and/or aerial work platforms so that they can be used optimally, efficiently and functionally.

Your tasks and responsibilities

  - Troubleshooting;

  - Analysing malfunctions;

  - Troubleshooting faults using electronic and hydraulic diagrams;

  - Performing maintenance checks;

  - Performing repairs;

  - Performing on-site inspections;

  - Keeping workplace/environment clean and tidy.

Our offer

  - Market-based salary and working conditions according to the Collective Labour Agreement for Metalworking;

  - We have a 40-hour working week and, according to the collective labour agreement, you can choose between the full commutation of ADV or 13 ADV days per year;

  - Discounts on products and services with the Employee Benefit Programme;

  - Free access to SnowWorld;

  - Holiday pay, training opportunities, bicycle plan, fitness plan, overtime compensation (free time or money), ...;

  - 26-leave days and the possibility to buy an additional 8 leave days;

  - Monthly Friday afternoon drinks in our in-house café;

  - The opportunity to attend various events for free;

  - Being part of our informal Collé family.

Your profile.

  - MBO working and thinking level, obtained through a technical education such as mechatronics or agricultural mechanisation;

  - Technical knowledge, experience and insight in the field of electro and hydraulics;

  - Problem-solving and analytical skills, service-oriented;

  - Sense of responsibility, flexible, independent and also a team player;

  - Sufficient command of the Dutch language. We also invite suitable candidates with a command of the English and/or German language who are willing to learn Dutch;

  - Living in the Sittard region.

Interested?
Don't wait any
